* series_dual_diode.lib
* Subcircuit models for series-connected dual diodes in SOT-23-3
*
* These parts have 3 pins: A (common anode of D1), AK (cathode of D1 / anode of D2), C (cathode of D2)
* D1: anode=pin1, cathode=pin3    D2: anode=pin3, cathode=pin2
*
* BAT54S  — dual Schottky series (SOT-23-3)
*   KiCad pins: 1=Anode, 2=cathode, 3=AK
*   KiCad Sim.Pins = "1 3 2"  (port order: a ak c)
*
* MMBD4148W-7-F — dual signal diode series (SOT-23-3)
*   KiCad pins: 1=Anode, 2=cathode, 3=AK
*   KiCad Sim.Pins = "1 3 2"  (port order: a ak c)

* Generic Schottky model (Vf ~0.3V, fast)
.model SCHOTTKY_GENERIC D (Is=1e-9 Rs=0.3 N=1.05 Tt=10n Cjo=5p Vj=0.5 M=0.4 Iave=200m)

* Generic fast signal diode model (approximates 1N4148 / 1N914)
.model SIGNAL_DIODE D (Is=2.2e-9 Rs=0.5 N=1.84 Tt=12n Cjo=4p Vj=0.5 M=0.33 Iave=200m)

* BAT54S: series dual Schottky
* Port order: a ak c
.subckt BAT54S a ak c
D1 a ak SCHOTTKY_GENERIC
D2 ak c SCHOTTKY_GENERIC
.ends BAT54S

* MMBD4148W-7-F: series dual signal diode
* Port order: a ak c
.subckt MMBD4148W a ak c
D1 a ak SIGNAL_DIODE
D2 ak c SIGNAL_DIODE
.ends MMBD4148W
